# EF Core 10 Breaking Changes for Your Code

## 1. `SetProperty` generic arity changed

In EF Core 10, `SetProperty` now requires **two** type arguments (`TEntity, TProperty`) instead of just `TProperty`. Your manual expression tree construction breaks because you're only passing one type argument.

**Fix:**

```csharp
// Before (EF Core 9)
typeArguments: new[] { typeof(string) },

// After (EF Core 10)
typeArguments: new[] { typeof(Blog), typeof(string) },
```

## 2. Complex type column naming conflicts

EF Core 10 no longer silently disambiguates columns when multiple complex properties share the same CLR type. You'll get a runtime error for duplicate column names (e.g., both `ShippingAddress` and `BillingAddress` have `Street`).

**Fix — explicitly configure column names:**

```csharp
modelBuilder.Entity<Customer>(b => {
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.ShippingAddress, sa => {
        sa.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("ShippingAddress_Street");
    });
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.BillingAddress, ba => {
        ba.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("BillingAddress_Street");
    });
});

// For nested: configure at each level
modelBuilder.Entity<Order>(b => {
    b.ComplexProperty(o => o.Payment, pay => {
        pay.ComplexProperty(p => p.BillingAddress, ba => {
            ba.Property(a => a.City).HasColumnName("Payment_BillingAddress_City");
        });
    });
});
```

## 3. `IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger` gained a `CommandSource` parameter

EF Core 10 added a `CommandSource` parameter to the diagnostics methods to indicate what triggered the command.

**Fix:**

```csharp
public class MyLogger : IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger
{
    public InterceptionResult<DbDataReader> CommandReaderExecuting(
        IRelationalConnection connection,
        DbCommand command,
        DbContext context,
        Guid commandId,
        Guid connectionId,
        DateTimeOffset startTime,
        CommandSource commandSource)   // ← new parameter
    { /* logging */ }
}
```

---

**Summary:** The theme across all three is EF Core 10 tightening generic signatures and adding context parameters. The expression-tree fix is a one-line change; complex types need explicit column config; the logger needs the new `CommandSource` argument on every method in the interface.
